---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '@/components/Container.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Zhixu Zhao on open systems, programming languages, and the freedom to change our tools.">
  <Container>
    <div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A little context</p><h1>About me</h1></div>
    <article class="prose">
      <p>I’m {site.name}, a systems engineer interested in programming languages, Linux, compilers, AI inference, and tools for open collaboration. I like software whose workings are available to the people who use it: something you can inspect, understand, and reshape when your needs change.</p>
      <p>Through <a href="/projects/#pyvivo">pyvivo</a> and my <a href="/projects/#emacs-d">Emacs configuration</a>, I explore live, programmable development environments: changing running programs and adapting my editor around AI agents and everyday workflows. <a href="/projects/#lightnet">LightNet</a>, TensorLight, and lightnet-plugin reflect my earlier work on neural-network optimization, compiler-style transformations, and extensible execution systems.</p>
      <p>I also write about the experience of building software: engineering taste, C and Lisp, AI-assisted development, and Emacs as an environment that can evolve while I’m using it. A recurring interest is the short path from noticing a problem in a tool to changing the tool itself.</p>
      <p>This site is a home for those projects and longer thoughts. My code is on <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a>, and I write in Chinese as Favoryoung on <a href={site.zhihu}>Zhihu</a>. If you’re exploring similar problems, I’d be glad to compare notes.</p>
    </article>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
